  "query_preview": "/FRIDAY THROUGH TUESDAY/...\nIssued at 205 PM CDT Wed Oct 7 2026\n\nFriday...The continued ongoing convergent LLJ processes will look to \ncontinue to be enough to keep some showers festering acrs the area \nfor much of the day until lifting off to the north and east Friday \nevening. Fcst soundings and profiles suggest a nice plume of 6.5+ \nC/km lapse rates and mid layer MUCAPEs of 500-1000 J/kg to support \nsome thunder. The latest ECMWF runs continue to suggest the Friday \nactivity will occur north of I-80 or even Hwy 30.  A LLVL warm \nfrontal retreat and more clouds/precip in the north will make for a \nchallenging temp forecast Friday and there could easily be at least \na 10 degree difference from the south to north.\n\nSaturday and Sunday...Digging longer wave upper trof acrs the \nPacific Northwest and ridging amplifying up the GRT LKS(aided by \nnorthward advancing subsidence fields off approaching Isaias) will \nresult in warming southwesterlies acrs the MID CONUS and toward the \nGRT LKS. Saturday will be a full blown warm sector day with breezy \nsoutherly winds and increasing thicknesses that support highs in the \n80s for much of the area, with mid 80s a good possibility. This may \nbe a day of increased cropland fire danger risk depending on \nhumidity trends. Then eyes turn to the tropical system from the Gulf \nand the path it may take getting drawn northward inland. How close \nthis system can make it to the local area by Sunday is still at \nquestion, but the latest trends don't vary too much from older model \nruns. Still a scenario to watch of course, as the local area sure \ndoes not need the precip off such a system.\n\nMonday through Wednesday...Depending on what or how the above system \nbehaves, early next week otherwise may be characterized by warm \nupper ridging and well above normal temp regime for Monday.  Upper \nridge retrograde with a passing cyclone pressing into the GRT LKS \nwill look to allow for a decent cold frontal passage and following \nlower level Canadian high pressure with a cool push dumping down \nthrough the area by Tuesday. This mid week cool down will be short \nlived as the upstream upper trof and associated lower level \ncyclogenesis blossoming and try too eject out toward the upper \nmidwest. If this unfolds this way, unsettled weather looks on tap \nlate next Wednesday into Thursday.",
